# EXAMPLE TEMPLATE -- do not put a real credential, ID, or hostname in this
# file. Every value below must be empty or an obviously-fake placeholder; a
# CI gate (scripts/check-example-file-leaks.sh) rejects any `.example` file
# containing a real-looking secret/ID pattern.
#
# Production secrets for the nightly task-runner Cloud Run Job
# (scripts/gcp-task-runner.sh). Copy to .env.task-runner.production.local
# and fill in the values. Never commit the copy (gitignored via .env*).
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line. Every non-empty KEY becomes a Secret
# Manager secret (task-runner-<key, lower-case, dashes>) exposed to the Job
# as the env var KEY. The file is parsed, not sourced.
#
# IMPORTANT: list EVERY production secret the app's scheduled-task handlers
# can read -- payment gateway keys, email/SMS provider keys, any third-party
# API key -- not just the database URL. Compare against the env vars
# configured on the deployed app (for example the Vercel project's
# production environment). A missing key only fails at run time, inside the
# handler that needs it.

# Required. Use the unpooled (direct) Neon connection string.
DATABASE_URL=
# CRON_SECRET is not needed here: the Job runs the tasks directly, not through
# the HTTP route that checks it.

# Add every other production secret the handlers use, for example:
# EXAMPLE_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
